# target: libs/JUCE
#
# Emscripten/WASM support for JUCE 8.0.12.
#
# JUCE 8 defines JUCE_WASM and ships juce_SystemStats_wasm.cpp, but the target is
# incomplete. This adds:
#
#   - the emscripten.h include and WASM thread-priority entries
#   - wasm-before-linux platform detection (host projects define LINUX)
#   - WASM branches in juce_core/juce_events/juce_graphics/juce_gui_basics
#     pointing at host/surge_wasm/
#   - NativeImageType for wasm, a PluginHostType case, a PropertiesFile case
#   - a narrowed posix guard so updateStatInfoForFile stays available
#   - firing timers from the synchronous pump
#
# That last one is the subtle one. JUCE decrements every timer's countdown from
# the timer THREAD's run loop, and an Emscripten build without -pthread never
# starts that thread -- so callPendingTimersSynchronously() found the first
# countdown still positive, broke out immediately, and no JUCE timer ever fired.
# Surge drives its entire editor from a 60 Hz timer, so the panel rendered but
# never refreshed anything idle-driven.
#
# All upstreamable.
diff --git a/modules/juce_audio_processors/utilities/juce_PluginHostType.cpp b/modules/juce_audio_processors/utilities/juce_PluginHostType.cpp
index 7ce6bf5..e96ffde 100644
